INT. VERIDIAN SYSTEMS - OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - FIRE DRILL - DAY

Rows of grey cubicles. A laminated sign reads "SYNERGY IS A VERB." Alarm bell clangs on a loop.

PERPETUA NWOSU (40s, headset, high-vis vest over a blazer) strides between desks with a clipboard. ALISTAIR BOONSRI (30s, sleeves rolled, mug in hand) does not stand. LOLA FIGUEROA-WREN (20s, intern, lanyard tangled) stares at a vending machine.

                    PERPETUA
          Everyone! Exit through the east stairwell! Walk, do not run!

Nobody else is there. The desks are empty. She says it anyway.

                    ALISTAIR
          Perpetua, we're the only two on this floor.

                    PERPETUA
          Three.

                    ALISTAIR
          Fine, three.

Lola still has not moved.

                    PERPETUA
          Lola. Stairwell.

                    LOLA
          I'm waiting for my pretzels.

                    PERPETUA
          There is a fire.

                    LOLA
          Then I'll be quick.

Alistair finally stands, mug still steaming.

                    ALISTAIR
          (muttering)
          Every quarter, a fire. Never an actual fire.

                    PERPETUA
          I heard that.

                    ALISTAIR
          It was for you to hear.

The alarm stops. Silence rings. Perpetua's headset crackles; she tilts her head, listens, goes still.

                    PERPETUA
          (to herself)
          Oh no.

                    ALISTAIR
          What?

                    PERPETUA
          It was a real fire. Floor four. They forgot to tell the drill coordinator.

                    LOLA
          (calling, bright)
          Everyone! Exit through the east stairwell!

Her pretzels thump into the tray. She grabs them and sprints. Perpetua and Alistair follow, mug abandoned, spilling steam onto carpet.

At the stairwell door, Perpetua stops, hand on the push bar.

                    PERPETUA
          False alarm. Floor four just burned a casserole.

                    ALISTAIR
          I hate this company.

                    LOLA
          (mouth full)
          Pretzel?
